;; Units made from OCaml sources that are written against the standard
;; library, checked against the Rocq semantics of Flambda 2 as those of the
;; directory above are (see README.md).
;;
;; For each X.ml here (with X.mli if there is one), X.fl is the term that
;; the compiler gives to Simplify, as ../from_ocaml.sh makes it when it is
;; given the directory of the standard library, and X.expected is what the
;; test tool prints of it. Both are kept. The rules, which gen_rules.sh
;; writes from the files that are here, make X.fl again and compare, and
;; run the tool on X.fl and compare. `dune promote` updates either.
;;
;; To add an example, add X.ml (and X.mli), X.fl and X.expected, and
;; nothing else. The rules are included by run/dune and not by this file.

(rule
 (deps
  (glob_files *.ml)
  (glob_files *.mli)
  (glob_files *.fl)
  (glob_files *.expected))
 (action
  (with-stdout-to
   dune.inc
   (run sh %{dep:gen_rules.sh} %{deps}))))
